/*This technique is called lazy removal. Expired indices are removed when they reach the top of the heap.
Priority queue vs. monotonic queue
Approach	Time	Space	Difficulty
Priority queue	O(n log n)	Up to O(n)	Simpler
Monotonic queue	O(n)	O(k)	More efficient
The monotonic queue is the optimal solution, but the priority-queue solution is also valid and often easier to understand.
